<article class="env-definition" id="03R3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03R3">Definition <span data-tag="03R3">59.61.3</span>.</a> Two finite central simple algebras $A_1$ and $A_2$ over $K$ are called <em>similar</em>, or <em>equivalent</em> if there exist $m, n \geq 1$ such that $\text{Mat}(n \times n, A_1) \cong \text{Mat}(m \times m, A_2)$. We write $A_1 \sim A_2$. </p>
